	(gr_text_box "Mechanical design notes \n=================\n\nThe height of the battery holders is 22 mm above the top side of the PCB, with the diameter of the 18650 batteries aligning to this level.\n\nOn the bottom side of the board, the tallest component is the coil, standing 8.5 mm above the PCB level, the JST-GH connectors are 5 mm high. The module's maximum thickness is therefore at the coil, measuring 22 + 1.6 + 8.5 mm = 32.1 mm.\n\nBattery contacts are directly accessible from the bottom side. The battery holder must be securely mounted with an insulating material that prevents potential shorting of contacts from below.\n\nTo prevent the batteries from slipping out of the holder unintentionally, a mechanical retention system is required on the top side, such as a surface above the module or a clamp. This retention solution must not cause mechanical damage to the battery casing, for example, due to vibrations.\n\nThe module is designed to be mounted through the battery holder's mounting holes using M3 countersunk screws. It is recommended to use DIN 7991 screws, and the module should be secured with at least four screws. Mounting holes are displayed in layout drawing\n\nThe 3-pin JST-GH output connector can be mounted in either the inward or outward orientation of the board, depending on the application and the module's positioning."
		(start 192.11 64.14)
		(end 273.81 141.04)
		(layer "Dwgs.User")
		(uuid "22abc160-e2b9-4778-8fed-c2c017872dcb")
